moon knight might not be the most  well-known marvel character but he's got  a rich history in the comics all the  same with a new mcu series about to drop  what do you need to know about the  character and the show before you watch  the official trailer for moon knight  premiered during the rams cardinals wild  card game in january 2022 and in  addition to providing fans with a sneak  peek of what the highly anticipated  series might entail it also revealed the  show's release date moon knight is  scheduled to premiere on wednesday march  30th 2022 and like the rest of marvel's  phase 4 tv series we'll stream  exclusively on disney plus as of right  now it's unclear what time the series  will become available for streaming but  we can speculate that it will be similar  to the release times prior marvel series  like hawkeye loki and wandavision which  all premiered their episodes at 3am  eastern time each week we also know that  moon knight will consist of six episodes  according to kevin feige the marvel  studios boss also says that these  episodes will run between 40 and 50  minutes which is in line with other  marvel disney plus series  leading the cast of moon knight is none  other than oscar isaac who is set to  play the titular hero as well as his  multitude of overlapping personalities  moon knight's true identity is that of  mark spector a mercenary who suffers  from dissociative identity disorder and  constantly swaps between several  distinctive identities as the series  goes on the interesting thing is that  these identities essentially function as  totally different characters and it'll  be interesting to see how isaac brings  them each to life on screen ethan hawke  is also set to appear in the series as a  cult leader named arthur harrow who  appears in the trailer and encourages  mark to  embrace the chaos  the series also features french actor  gaspard yuliao who appears posthumously  as anton mogart the alter ego of the  character known as midnight man yuliel  tragically passed away in a ski accident  after filming and moon knight was one of  the last projects he ever worked on  others confirmed to be in the series  include f marie abraham who voices the  egyptian god kanshu lucy thakuray who  plays a co-worker who is close to one of  mark's many personalities and may calla  maui in an undisclosed role  the official trailer for moon knight  revealed quite a lot about the story and  characters that we'll be seeing  throughout the series at the start of  the trailer mark believes himself to be  a man named steven who works at a museum  and admits that he can't tell the  difference between life and dreams he is  tormented by strange visions and  nightmares and doesn't even recognize  the name mark when somebody calls him on  the phone what's wrong with you mark  why did you call me mark  mark's story is as much about fighting  literal bad guys as it is about fighting  his inner thoughts and from what we see  in this trailer it seems like the latter  is a losing battle after a brief montage  of mark's disturbing visions we finally  get to see him don moon knight's iconic  white costume the suit literally  materializes from thin air around mark  as he looks up at the moon indicating  that similar to the comics he receives  his powers from the egyptian god of the  moon khanshu finally the trailer ends  with mark brutally beating some  monstrous looking creature before  turning to the camera it's an incredible  trailer from start to finish giving fans  just enough to be excited about without  giving too much away in regards to the  plot for now it looks like moon knight  is going to have two villains dr arthur  harrow and midnight man it seems as if  the latter will be more of a secondary  baddie as ethan hawk's hero looks to be  the main villain of the series  however it's suspected that there's more  than meets the eye here given that dr  harrow has only appeared in one comic  book issue there's not that much story  in the comic for the show to pull from  either many fans believe the persona of  dr harrow is a red herring and hawk is  actually playing the moon knight villain  sun king a former ravencroft institute  patient sun king has a base of loyal  followers much like we see hawks pharaoh  have in the trailer  both sun king and moon knight have  connections to egyptian gods with the  former obsessed with aman ra and the  latter who is blessed with powers by  kanchu it's also very possible that  hawke's character is an amalgamation of  dr harrow sun king and other famous moon  knight villains only time will tell what  we do know for certain is the  inspiration for hawk's character in an  interview with seth meyers hawk pointed  to one famous cult leader as the  inspiration for his portrayal of dr  harrow  i've based my character on david correct  have you really  yes  moon knight will feature three directors  one of whom directed four episodes while  the remaining pair directed the other  two according to the hollywood reporter  muhammad diab is helming four episodes  solo marking the first time he's  directed an english language project  diab is known in his home country of  egypt for projects like cairo 678 and  clash  but moon knight marks his first  hollywood project per variety the famous  directing duo of justin benson and aaron  morehead tackled the other two episodes  the indie horror visionaries don't have  the longest resumes in the business but  their work speaks for itself they  directed 2019's synchronic with anthony  mackie an episode of jordan peele's  twilight zone reboot and 2017's the  endless in which they also starred the  higher-ups at marvel studios clearly  have been impressed with the work  they've seen from benson and morehead as  the pair have also been brought on to  direct a majority of the episodes from  the upcoming loki season 2 according to  deadline  so far every mcu series on disney plus  has been scripted by a different writer  moon knight will introduce head writer  jeremy slater to the marvel cinematic  universe but this is far from slater's  first dip in the superhero pool he  penned the script to the 2015 fantastic  four movie he's also one of the creators  of netflix's the umbrella academy if  moon knight turns out to be anything  like slater's initial pitch we're in for  a treat he told empire raiders of the  lost ark was actually a big reference  when i first pitched how can we tell  this dark complex story but also inject  some big fun supernatural amblin style  magic at the same time a lot of trust  has been put into slater recently which  gives us a lot of hope for moon knight  he's also painting the script for mortal  kombat 2.  leading into the premiere there's no  clear answer on where moon knight fits  in the official timeline of the marvel  cinematic universe as of now hawkeye is  the latest show on the timeline taking  place in december 2024 it's entirely  possible that moon night is the first  mcu project to occur in 2025 if it takes  place right after hawkeye it's also  possible moon night happens sometime  during 2023 as do two other disney plus  live action series one division begins  three weeks after the conclusion of  avengers end game while the falcon in  the winter soldier is about six months  out loki kicks off in 2012 but about 99  percent of the series occurs in a space  outside of time so it really doesn't  have a solid place on the timeline  eternals shanxi and the legend of the  ten rings and spider-man no way home all  take place before hawkeye with no way  home definitely landing in 2023 long  story short moon knight can fit anywhere  every mcu disney plus series has its own  identity but moon knight is going to  really shake things up in a big way  kevin feige admitted to empire that  things are taking a major left turn with  moon knight suggesting it's the darkest  series in the mcu to date he told the  outlet it's been fun to work with disney  plus and see the boundaries shifting on  what we're able to do there are moments  when moon knight is wailing on another  character and it is loud and brutal and  the knee-jerk reaction is we're gonna  pull back on this right we're not  pulling back there's a tonal shift this  is a different thing  so far every mcu series has held a tv 14  rating including the animated project  what if the way feige describes moon  knight and its brutality sounds like the  series might have earned a more adult  rating than its predecessors but disney  plus has labeled it with the tv 14  rating on its website one thing is clear  moon knight is certainly going to push  the barriers of how far a tv 14 show can  go  for now it looks like there won't be a  second season of moon night but that's  based on a small comment made by oscar  isaac when speaking with jared leto for  variety's actors on actors series isaac  mentioned that moon knight was a limited  series limited means just that so for  now fans likely shouldn't get their  hopes up for a second season wandavision  was also confirmed to be just a limited  series but that's not the case for all  mcu live-action shows so far loki is the  only disney plus series for marvel to  have confirmed to season 2. this  announcement came in the credits of the  first season's finale episode so if we  are getting a follow-up for moon knight  its finale could be the episode that  holds all the answers however just  because there might not be a season two  of the series that doesn't mean we won't  be seeing moon knight again in the mcu  up to this point the title characters of  every mcu series had already appeared in  multiple movies so there was always the  assumption we'd see them again on the  big screen moon knight is the first  title character to get their origin  story in the disney plus series and his  future afterward is slightly unknown  since we know we probably won't be  getting a season 2 we'd have to hope  oscar isaac's mark spector would show up  in future mcu flicks and it looks like  those hopes are due to be fulfilled  kevin feige confirmed to the hollywood  reporter that moon knight would appear  in an mcu film after the series this is  also the case for jennifer walters from  she-hulk and kamala khan from ms marvel  for now your guess is as good as ours as  far as to where moon knight might appear  next but hopefully we'll get some clues  during the show's six episode run he  isn't one of the characters rumored to  appear in doctor strange in the  multiverse of madness and there have  been no rumblings of him showing up in  thor love and thunder or black panther  wakanda forever there's no shortage of  upcoming mcu movies though so here's  hoping we'll get more moon knight sooner  than later  cameos in the mcu are common these days  and the disney plus marvel series are no  exception james rhodes popped up in an  emmy nominated scene in the falcon in  the winter soldier wilson fisk made his  mcu debut in hawkeye the x-men's version  of pietro maximoff sword of cameoed in  one division and chris hemsworth had a  very sneaky voice cameo in loki as a  trapped frog thor  needless to say we are expecting someone  we know to show up in moon night rumors  abound that jon bernthal could be  reprising his role as frank castle aka  the punisher in moon knight redditors  have been hoping for this cameo for a  while now especially given that frank  castle and moon knight have a history in  the comics with vincent d'onofrio  showing up on disney plus in an old  netflix role it's certainly possible  there's also speculation that mark  ruffalo might be appearing as bruce  banner in moon knight after he was  spotted in budapest hungary during the  same time the series was filming there  if that's true it seems like there'd be  no better mcu hero to teach moon knight  how to control his emotional issues  that's my secret captain  i'm always angry  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite mcu series are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you

